<title>EGYPT: Egypt buys 30,000T of soybean for $296/tonne C&amp;F.</title>
<headline>Egypt buys 30,000T of soybean for $296/tonne C&amp;F.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egypt has bought 30,000 tonnes of soybean from the Swiss company Romak for $296 C&amp;F per tonne for delivery in the first half of December, an official from the state Holding Company for Food Industries said on Wednesday .</p>
<p>Head of Sales Muharram Ghanem said that the shipment had a buyer's option of plus or minus five percent.</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
